p.src:
The leading fermionic correction is therefore $\delta m_{\phi,F}^2
\sim -C_F\frac{g^2}{\delta^2}
=-C_Fg^2\Lambda^2,$ where $C_F>0$ contains numerical, spin, and multiplicity factors. The scalar loop has the corresponding form $\delta m_{\phi,B}^2
\sim+C_B\frac{\lambda}{\delta^2}
=+C_B\lambda\Lambda^2.$ We have not yet solved the fine-tuning problem, but we have found something indispensable: a contribution with the same ultraviolet degree and the opposite sign.

